(Discrepancy 3: undocumented asymmetry - byte WRITE bounds are checked against capacity, and a write past current size but within capacity silently EXTENDS the length. Byte READ bounds are checked against current size, so a read at that same now-valid-by-write index still errors if size has not caught up. This single probe shows both halves together, as originally hand-run.)
(expected output:
6
0
read at capacity edge errored
0
)
a buffer called fx is 8 bytes in size.
append "ABCD" to fx.
Set byte 6 of fx to 88.
print fx's size.
a number called g is byte 5 of fx.
On error print "gap read errored".
print g.
a number called atcap is byte 8 of fx.
On error print "read at capacity edge errored".
print atcap.
